## Conclusion

This project demonstrates how traditional frequency-based NLP techniques can be used to build autocomplete and autocorrect systems. The results also highlight the limitations of simple statistical approaches compared with modern production systems such as Google Keyboard, which use larger datasets, contextual models, personalised information, and more advanced machine-learning techniques.

